// Non-decency conservation (L. 843-1..7, R. 843-1..8): the organism keeps
// the allocation up to 18 months, notifies the owner, the tenant pays a
// reduced rent under eviction immunity, unconformed sums are lost to the
// owner, exceptional maintenance on the five R. 843-6 grounds renewable
// once, new-tenant conservation on a fresh finding (6 months), owner refund
// of the above-rent excess, hotel/accession derogations with board, prefect
// and committee notices, and the narrow L. 843-7 qualified-portfolio
// continuation. Allocation-only (ALF/ALS).
// Effects without a producer below (non_resiliation_bail_non_decence,
// non_recours_proprietaire_loyer) hold as immunity effects, not standalone
// derivations; if LDC flags producer-less relations, the reviewer converts
// them to empirical case attestations.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.apl version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:apl";

